  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: integer overflow in the pixel cache staging buffer size\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106571.patch: use overflow-checked\n       multiplications for the staging buffer size in\n       SetPixelCacheNexusPixels() in magick/cache.c\n     - CVE-2026-106571\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: coder security policy bypass\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106579.patch: check the coder name against the\n       coder policy at all four decoder and encoder calls, including the\n       WriteImage() fallback, in magick/constitute.c\n     - CVE-2026-106579\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: PostScript code injection through image labels\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106577.patch: escape parentheses and backslashes\n       in, and trim, the labels written by the PS, PS2, PS3 and PDF coders in\n       coders/ps.c, coders/ps2.c, coders/ps3.c and coders/pdf.c\n     - CVE-2026-106577",
